IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa25-part40.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 40 "Company directors: foreign disqualification etc":
-- ss 1182 to 1191 (lines 16661-16782 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- What this Part is. Sections 1184 to 1191 give the Secretary of State powers to make regulations (disqualifying
-- persons subject to foreign restrictions, making them liable for a company's debts, requiring statements to the
-- registrar, creating offences): regulation-making powers and their procedure are inert, reason 2 (NOTES.md). What is
-- encoded is what the text itself defines or fixes: "subject to foreign restrictions" (s 1182), "the court" and "UK
-- company" (s 1183), "disqualification undertaking" and "person disqualified under this Part" (s 1184(3), (4)), the
-- ceilings on the penalties the regulations may provide (ss 1186(2)-(3), 1191(2)-(3)), joint and several liability
-- and "involved in the management" (s 1187(2), (3)) and "specified" (s 1190(5)). No regulations under this Part are
-- among the sources: every answer says only what the Act itself says.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent, list not closed,
--               includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every name below begins with the section label it implements.

§ `Part 40: company directors, foreign disqualification etc`

§§ `Introductory`

-- ---- s 1182: Persons subject to foreign restrictions ----------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1182 activity` IS ONE OF
    `s 1182 being a director of a company`
    `s 1182 acting as receiver of a company's property`
    `s 1182 being concerned or taking part in the promotion, formation or management of a company`
    `s 1182 any other activity`

-- src:16674 | (3) The references in subsection (2) to acting in connection with the affairs of a company are to doing any of the following—
-- src:16675 | (a) being a director of a company,
-- src:16676 | (b) acting as receiver of a company's property, or
-- src:16677 | (c) being concerned or taking part in the promotion, formation or management of a company.
@ref s 1182(3) Acting in connection with the affairs of a company (src:16674-16677)
GIVEN activity IS A `s 1182 activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1182(3) the activity is acting in connection with the affairs of a company` MEANS
    CONSIDER activity
    WHEN `s 1182 any other activity` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The references in subsection (2) to acting in connection with the affairs of a company are to doing any of the following— (a) being a director of a company, (b) acting as receiver of a company's property, or (c) being concerned or taking part in the promotion, formation or management of a company"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16665 | (2) A person is subject to foreign restrictions if under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom—
-- src:16666 | (a) he is, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, disqualified to any extent from acting in connection with the affairs of a company,
-- src:16667 | (b) he is, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, required—
-- src:16668 | (i) to obtain permission from a court or other authority, or
-- src:16669 | (ii) to meet any other condition,
-- src:16670 | before acting in connection with the affairs of a company, or
-- src:16671 | (c) he has, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, given undertakings to a court or other authority of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom—
-- src:16672 | (i) not to act in connection with the affairs of a company, or
-- src:16673 | (ii) restricting the extent to which, or the way in which, he may do so.
@ref s 1182(2) A person is subject to foreign restrictions (src:16665-16673)
GIVEN `the restriction is under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      activity IS A `s 1182 activity`
      `by reason of misconduct or unfitness he is disqualified to any extent from the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of misconduct or unfitness he is required to obtain permission from a court or other authority, or to meet any other condition, before the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of misconduct or unfitness he has given undertakings to a court or other authority of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom not to do the activity, or restricting the extent to which or the way in which he may do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1182(2) the person is subject to foreign restrictions` MEANS
    IF `the restriction is under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
       AND `s 1182(3) the activity is acting in connection with the affairs of a company` activity EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (    `by reason of misconduct or unfitness he is disqualified to any extent from the activity`
             OR `by reason of misconduct or unfitness he is required to obtain permission from a court or other authority, or to meet any other condition, before the activity`
             OR `by reason of misconduct or unfitness he has given undertakings to a court or other authority of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom not to do the activity, or restricting the extent to which or the way in which he may do so`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is subject to foreign restrictions if under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom— (a) he is, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, disqualified ..., (b) he is, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, required ..., or (c) he has, by reason of misconduct or unfitness, given undertakings ..." (an "if" that is not met: marginal reading (a))

-- "company" means a company incorporated or formed under the law of the country or territory in question.
-- src:16678 | (4) In this section—
-- src:16679 | (a) “company” means a company incorporated or formed under the law of the country or territory in question, and
@ref s 1182(4)(a) "Company" (src:16678-16679)
GIVEN `the body is incorporated or formed under the law of the country or territory in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1182(4)(a) the body is a company for the purposes of s 1182` MEANS
    IF `the body is incorporated or formed under the law of the country or territory in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means a company incorporated or formed under the law of the country or territory in question"

-- "director" means the holder of an office corresponding to that of director of a UK company; "receiver" includes any
-- corresponding officer under the law of that country or territory.
-- src:16680 | (b) in relation to such a company—
-- src:16681 | “director” means the holder of an office corresponding to that of director of a UK company; and
@ref s 1182(4)(b) "Director" (src:16680-16681)
GIVEN `the office corresponds to that of director of a UK company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1182(4)(b) the person is a director of the company` MEANS
    IF `the office corresponds to that of director of a UK company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“director” means the holder of an office corresponding to that of director of a UK company"

-- src:16680 | (b) in relation to such a company—
-- src:16682 | “receiver” includes any corresponding officer under the law of that country or territory.
@ref s 1182(4)(b) "Receiver" (src:16680-16682)
GIVEN `the officer is a receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is a corresponding officer under the law of that country or territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1182(4)(b) the officer is a receiver of the company` MEANS
    IF `the officer is a receiver` OR `the officer is a corresponding officer under the law of that country or territory`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“receiver” includes any corresponding officer under the law of that country or territory"

-- ---- s 1183: Meaning of "the court" and "UK company" ---------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1183 court` IS ONE OF
    `s 1183 the High Court in England and Wales`
    `s 1183 the county court`
    `s 1183 the Court of Session`
    `s 1183 the sheriff court`
    `s 1183 the High Court in Northern Ireland`

-- src:16683 | 1183 Meaning of “the court” and “UK company”
-- src:16684 | In this Part—
-- src:16685 | “the court” means—
-- src:16686 | (a) in England and Wales, the High Court or the county court;
-- src:16687 | (b) in Scotland, the Court of Session or the sheriff court;
-- src:16688 | (c) in Northern Ireland, the High Court;
@ref s 1183 "The court" in Part 40 (src:16683-16688)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 1183 court`
`s 1183 the courts that are "the court" in Part 40 for the part of the United Kingdom` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN LIST `s 1183 the High Court in England and Wales`, `s 1183 the county court`
    WHEN Scotland THEN LIST `s 1183 the Court of Session`, `s 1183 the sheriff court`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN LIST `s 1183 the High Court in Northern Ireland`

-- src:16683 | 1183 Meaning of “the court” and “UK company”
-- src:16684 | In this Part—
-- src:16685 | “the court” means—
-- src:16686 | (a) in England and Wales, the High Court or the county court;
-- src:16687 | (b) in Scotland, the Court of Session or the sheriff court;
-- src:16688 | (c) in Northern Ireland, the High Court;
@ref s 1183 "The court" in Part 40 (src:16683-16688)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      tribunal IS A `s 1183 court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1183 the tribunal is the court` MEANS
    IF elem tribunal (`s 1183 the courts that are "the court" in Part 40 for the part of the United Kingdom` place)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part “the court” means— (a) in England and Wales, the High Court or the county court; (b) in Scotland, the Court of Session or the sheriff court; (c) in Northern Ireland, the High Court"

-- src:16684 | In this Part—
-- src:16689 | “UK company” means a company registered under this Act.
@ref s 1183 "UK company" (src:16684-16689)
GIVEN `the company is registered under the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1183 the company is a UK company` MEANS
    IF `the company is registered under the Companies Act 2006`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“UK company” means a company registered under this Act"

§§ `Power to disqualify`

-- ---- s 1184: the definitions inside the power -------------------------------------------------------------
-- The power to make the regulations (subsections (1), (2), (5), (6), (7)) is inert, reason 2.

-- src:16699 | (3) The regulations may provide that the Secretary of State may accept an undertaking (a “disqualification undertaking”) from a person subject to foreign restrictions that he will not do anything which would be in breach of a disqualification under subsection (1).
@ref s 1184(3) "Disqualification undertaking" (src:16699)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has accepted the undertaking under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is from a person subject to foreign restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is that he will not do anything which would be in breach of a disqualification under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1184(3) the undertaking is a disqualification undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has accepted the undertaking under the regulations`
       AND `the undertaking is from a person subject to foreign restrictions`
       AND `the undertaking is that he will not do anything which would be in breach of a disqualification under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an undertaking (a “disqualification undertaking”) from a person subject to foreign restrictions that he will not do anything which would be in breach of a disqualification under subsection (1)" (a defined term: fork F10)

-- src:16700 | (4) In this Part—
-- src:16701 | (a) a “person disqualified under this Part” is a person—
-- src:16702 | (i) disqualified as mentioned in subsection (2)(a) or (b), or
-- src:16703 | (ii) who has given and is subject to a disqualification undertaking;
-- src:16704 | (b) references to a breach of a disqualification include a breach of a disqualification undertaking.
@ref s 1184(4)(a) "Person disqualified under this Part" (src:16700-16704)
GIVEN `he is disqualified automatically by virtue of the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he is disqualified by order of the court on the application of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has given and is subject to a disqualification undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1184(4)(a) the person is a person disqualified under this Part` MEANS
    IF `he is disqualified automatically by virtue of the regulations`
       OR `he is disqualified by order of the court on the application of the Secretary of State`
       OR `he has given and is subject to a disqualification undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “person disqualified under this Part” is a person— (i) disqualified as mentioned in subsection (2)(a) or (b), or (ii) who has given and is subject to a disqualification undertaking"

-- src:16700 | (4) In this Part—
-- src:16704 | (b) references to a breach of a disqualification include a breach of a disqualification undertaking.
@ref s 1184(4)(b) References to a breach of a disqualification (src:16700-16704)
GIVEN `the act is a breach of a disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is a breach of a disqualification undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1184(4)(b) the act is a breach of a disqualification` MEANS
    IF `the act is a breach of a disqualification` OR `the act is a breach of a disqualification undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to a breach of a disqualification include a breach of a disqualification undertaking"

-- ---- s 1186(2) and (3): the penalty the regulations may provide for breach of a disqualification ---------------
-- The most the regulations may provide. "the general limit in a magistrates' court" is not stated in the Act: the months
-- are an INPUT (never a number from memory). In relation to an offence committed before 2 May 2022 the limit is six
-- months (subsection (3)).

-- src:16727 | (2) The regulations may provide that a person guilty of such an offence is liable—
-- src:16728 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:16729 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:16730 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:16731 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
-- src:16732 | (3) In relation to an offence committed before 2 May 2022, for “the general limit in a magistrates’ court” in subsection (2)(b)(i) substitute “ six months ”.
@ref s 1186(2) The ceiling on the penalties the regulations may provide (src:16727-16732)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1186(2) the greatest penalty that the regulations may provide` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS (IF `the date the offence was committed` LESS THAN (Date 2 5 2022) THEN 6 ELSE `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`), unit IS Months)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the part of the United Kingdom is not stated

§§ `Power to make persons liable for company's debts`

-- ---- s 1187: Personal liability for debts of company ------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1187 other person` IS ONE OF
    `s 1187 the company`
    `s 1187 another person who is liable for the debts and liabilities, by virtue of s 1187 or otherwise`
    `s 1187 someone else`

-- src:16739 | (2) A person who is personally responsible by virtue of this section for debts and other liabilities of a company is jointly and severally liable in respect of those debts and liabilities with—
-- src:16740 | (a) the company, and
-- src:16741 | (b) any other person who (whether by virtue of this section or otherwise) is so liable.
@ref s 1187(2) Joint and several liability (src:16739-16741)
GIVEN `the person is personally responsible by virtue of s 1187 for debts and other liabilities of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A `s 1187 other person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1187(2) the person is jointly and severally liable with the other` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is personally responsible by virtue of s 1187 for debts and other liabilities of the company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is personally responsible by virtue of this section for debts and other liabilities of a company"
    ELSE CONSIDER other
         WHEN `s 1187 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "jointly and severally liable ... with— (a) the company, and (b) any other person who (whether by virtue of this section or otherwise) is so liable"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16742 | (3) For the purposes of this section a person is involved in the management of a company if he is concerned, whether directly or indirectly, or takes part, in the management of the company.
@ref s 1187(3) "Involved in the management of a company" (src:16742)
GIVEN `he is concerned, whether directly or indirectly, in the management of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he takes part in the management of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1187(3) the person is involved in the management of the company` MEANS
    IF `he is concerned, whether directly or indirectly, in the management of the company` OR `he takes part in the management of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is involved in the management of a company if he is concerned, whether directly or indirectly, or takes part, in the management of the company" (an "if" that is not met: marginal reading (a))

-- ---- s 1190: "specified" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16772 | (5) In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations.
@ref s 1190(5) "Specified" (src:16772)
GIVEN `the matter is specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1190(5) the matter is specified` MEANS
    IF `the matter is specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations"

-- ---- s 1191(2) and (3): the penalty the regulations may provide for the offences of failing to send a statement or sending
-- a false one. The same ceiling as s 1186(2)-(3): "the general limit in a magistrates' court" is an input; six months for an
-- offence committed before 2 May 2022 (subsection (3)).

-- src:16777 | (2) The regulations may provide that a person guilty of such an offence is liable—
-- src:16778 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:16779 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:16780 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:16781 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
-- src:16782 | (3) In relation to an offence committed before 2 May 2022, for “the general limit in a magistrates’ court” in subsection (2)(b)(i) substitute “ six months ”.
@ref s 1191(2) The ceiling on the penalties the regulations may provide (src:16777-16782)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1191(2) the greatest penalty that the regulations may provide` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS (IF `the date the offence was committed` LESS THAN (Date 2 5 2022) THEN 6 ELSE `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`), unit IS Months)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the part of the United Kingdom is not stated
